Allwinner "sunxi-drm" display driver (module sunxidrm), HDMI path only, for
the Allwinner A733 (sun60iw2): DRM core glue, CRTC/planes, display engine
v352, TCON-TV behind tcon-top, Synopsys DesignWare HDMI 2.0 TX with the
Synopsys PHY and the Allwinner top PHY, DMA GEM.

Source: https://github.com/alexcaoys/allwinner-bsp (branch linux-6.18.y)
Commit: 656a550c826787e7e72fae58ca793df9e0988ac8
Paths:  drivers/drm/...   -> this directory, same relative paths
        include/video/... -> bsp-include/video/...
        (sha256 of the unmodified files in UPSTREAM.sha256, paths relative
        to the upstream repository root)
License: GPL-2.0 per file (MODULE_LICENSE "GPL").

Status: builds against 7.3.3-300.fc45.aarch64 (modpost clean). Packaged
as cubie-a7a-display (DKMS); loaded by cubie-a7a-hat.service after
sun55i-pck600. First run on hardware 2026-11-11 (pass-2b boot): binds
tcon-top, DE, HDMI and tcon-tv and modesets HDMI-A-1 at 1366x768.

Imported (174 files): sunxi_drm_{drv,crtc,intf,notify,gem,debug,trace,hdmi},
sunxi_device/sunxi_{hdmi,tcon,tcon_top}, sunxi_device/hardware/include.h,
all of lowlevel_de and lowlevel_tcon, lowlevel_hdmi20 without dw_hdcp22.c
and esm_lib, from lowlevel_lcd tcon_lcd.[ch] with the headers it pulls in
(tcon_lcd_type.h, dsc_type.h, dsi_v1.h, dsi_v1_type.h), and the four
include/video headers the code includes.

Left out:
  - DSI, LVDS, RGB, eDP/DP, panel/, phy/ (DSI combo PHY), lib/ (SHA for DP
    HDCP), kernel_panic_printf.c, error_img.h, fonts.h
  - the vendor fbdev (sunxi_drmfb_core.c, sunxi_fbdev_platform.c,
    sunxi_fbdev_core.c, sunxi_fbdev.h): replaced by the kernel's generic
    fbdev client
  - HDCP 2.x (dw_hdcp22.c, esm_lib/): needs the vendor ESM firmware image
  - the vendor Makefiles and Kconfig: replaced by Makefile and a733-config.h

Kept although not on the A733 path, because shared files reference them:
  - lowlevel_lcd/tcon_lcd.c (sunxi_tcon.c serves tcon-lcd and tcon-tv)
  - lowlevel_hdmi20/phy_aw.c, phy_inno.c (sunxi_hdmi.c's platform table)
  - lowlevel_hdmi20/dw_hdcp.c (HDCP 1.x; also pins the controller's data
    path, so it is built; enabling HDCP is a DT property and is off)

New files (GPL-2.0-only):
  - Makefile, dkms.conf
  - a733-config.h: the Kconfig-style defines of this build; undefines
    CONFIG_EXTCON for this module so the HDMI code's extcon hot-plug
    reporting, which needs the private drivers/extcon/extcon.h, is not built
  - compat/mainline-compat.h: drm_atomic_state -> drm_atomic_commit renames
  - compat/sunxi-sid.h, compat/sunxi-iommu.h, compat/sunxi-gpio.h: stand-ins
    for vendor-kernel headers
  - compat/bsp_stubs.c: sunxi_get_soc_ver()/sunxi_get_soc_markid() returning
    0, the dw_hdcp2x_* entry points (path override/readback are the vendor's
    two register accesses, the rest report "not available"), and a module
    soft dependency on sun55i-pck600

Changes to imported files:
  - sunxi_drm_drv.c: sunxi_fbdev_init() declaration and call removed;
    DRM_FBDEV_DMA_DRIVER_OPS added to the drm_driver and drm_client_setup()
    called after drm_dev_register()
  - sunxi_drm_drv.c: sunxi_drm_bind() calls
    aperture_remove_all_conflicting_devices() after component_bind_all(),
    so the EFI GOP simple-framebuffer (simpledrm fb0) is removed before
    drm_dev_register()/drm_client_setup() and fbcon takes over the
    sunxi-drm fbdev
  - sunxi_drm_drv.c: sunxi_drm_offline_mode_pre_init() (DE write-back
    "offline" composition, not boot-logo code) is built only with
    CONFIG_AW_DRM_DE_OFFLINE_MODE, which a733-config.h leaves off; without
    it the DE call is an -EPERM stub and the function only logged
    "*ERROR* offline mode: init connecting not found" when no display was
    connected at bind
  - sunxi_drm_notify.c: __sunxi_disp_notify.disp_work is initialised
    statically (sunxi_disp_notify_init() is never called), so the exported
    async sunxi_disp_notify_call_chain() cannot queue an uninitialised work
  - sunxi_drm_trace.h: __assign_str() takes one argument
  - sunxi_device/hardware/lowlevel_de/sunxi_de.c: devfreq governor header is
    <linux/devfreq-governor.h>
  - sunxi_device/sunxi_hdmi.c: platform table also matches the root
    compatible "allwinner,sun60i-a733"
  - sunxi_device/hardware/lowlevel_hdmi20/phy_snps.c: snps_phy_init()
    counts the optional "snps_phy" DT table in a signed int (a missing
    property is -EINVAL, which as u32 sized a 16 GiB kmalloc and a bogus
    drive_size), checks the cell count, allocates count u32s with kcalloc,
    frees the buffer on a read error and sets drive_size only on success
  - Linux 7.4 (2026-11-18; builds against 7.3.4-300.fc45 and
    7.4.0-0.rc3.26.fc46, not run on a board with 7.4):
    - compat/drm/drm_fb_helper.h (new): 7.4 moved <drm/drm_fb_helper.h> to
      <drm/clients/drm_fbdev_helper.h>; found only where the kernel lacks
      the old name (compat/ follows the kernel's include directories)
    - sunxi_drm_crtc.c: 7.4 dropped drm_crtc_funcs.reset,
      drm_plane_funcs.reset and the __drm_atomic_helper_{crtc,plane}_reset()
      helpers; the core builds the initial state through
      .atomic_create_state. The state setup of sunxi_crtc_reset() and
      sunxi_atomic_plane_reset() moved into sunxi_crtc_alloc_state() and
      sunxi_plane_alloc_state(), used by .atomic_create_state on 7.4 and by
      the reset functions before. The plane reset no longer calls kfree()
      on an uninitialised pointer when the plane has no state yet, and
      neither reset dereferences a failed allocation
    - sunxi_drm_hdmi.c: drm_simple_encoder_init() (removed in 7.4) replaced
      by drm_encoder_init() with a cleanup-only drm_encoder_funcs, which is
      what the helper did

Device tree: fedora/dts/cubie-a7a-display.dtsi (included from binding stamp
15, cubie-a7a-dtb 0.10) describes the nodes
with this tree's CCU, reset and PPU references; the driver takes clocks,
resets, regulators and power domains through the generic kernel interfaces
by name, so no code change was needed for that.
